{"book":"shapes-2d","bookTitle":"2D shapes","concept":4,"title":"Kinds of quadrilaterals","grades":"Grades 6–8","goal":"I can name quadrilaterals by their properties and see how they are related.","teach":"<b>Trapezium:</b> one pair of parallel sides. <b>Parallelogram:</b> both pairs of opposite sides parallel (and equal). <b>Rectangle:</b> a parallelogram with four right angles. <b>Rhombus:</b> a parallelogram with four equal sides. <b>Square:</b> a rectangle and a rhombus at once. <b>Kite:</b> two pairs of equal sides next to each other. So every square is a rectangle, but not every rectangle is a square.","tvis":"<div class=\"vis\"><span class=\"vi\"><span style=\"display:inline-block;text-align:center;margin:0 4px\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" style=\"width:291px;height:auto\" viewBox=\"0 0 224 124\"><g transform=\"translate(12.0,2.0)\"><polygon points=\"10.0,100.0 150.0,100.0 190.0,20.0 50.0,20.0\" fill=\"#E3D6CE\" stroke=\"none\"/><line x1=\"10.0\" y1=\"100.0\" x2=\"150.0\" y2=\"100.0\" stroke=\"#555555\" stroke-width=\"1.6\"/><line x1=\"150.0\" y1=\"100.0\" x2=\"190.0\" y2=\"20.0\" stroke=\"#555555\" stroke-width=\"1.6\"/><line x1=\"190.0\" y1=\"20.0\" x2=\"50.0\" y2=\"20.0\" stroke=\"#555555\" stroke-width=\"1.6\"/><line x1=\"50.0\" y1=\"20.0\" x2=\"10.0\" y2=\"100.0\" stroke=\"#555555\" stroke-width=\"1.6\"/><line x1=\"77.5\" y1=\"94.0\" x2=\"77.5\" y2=\"106.0\" stroke=\"#7A0000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><line x1=\"82.5\" y1=\"94.0\" x2=\"82.5\" y2=\"106.0\" stroke=\"#7A0000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><line x1=\"122.5\" y1=\"26.0\" x2=\"122.5\" y2=\"14.0\" stroke=\"#7A0000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><line x1=\"117.5\" y1=\"26.0\" x2=\"117.5\" y2=\"14.0\" stroke=\"#7A0000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><line x1=\"164.6\" y1=\"57.3\" x2=\"175.4\" y2=\"62.7\" stroke=\"#7A0000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><line x1=\"35.4\" y1=\"62.7\" x2=\"24.6\" y2=\"57.3\" stroke=\"#7A0000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><path d=\"M74.0,105.0 L80.0,100.0 L74.0,95.0\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\