></g></svg><br><span style=\"font-size:9pt\">kite</span></span></span></div>","ex":{"q":"A quadrilateral has four equal sides and no right angles. Name it.","steps":["Four equal sides: a rhombus or a square.","A square has right angles; this shape has none.","It is a rhombus."]},"watch":"Arrows show parallel sides; ticks show equal sides. Use the marks, not how the shape looks.","qs":[{"text":"A rectangle is 8 cm long and 5 cm wide. Find its perimeter.","vis":"","parts":[{"t":"box","label":"Perimeter (cm)","a":"26","form":"val","o":null}],"hint":"2 × (8 + 5)","steps":"1. Formula: perimeter of a rectangle P = 2 × (l + b), where l is the length and b the breadth.<br>2. P = 2 × (8 + 5)<br>3. = 2 × 13 = 26 cm"},{"text":"One angle of a parallelogram is 65°. What size is the opposite angle?","vis":"","parts":[{"t":"box","label":"Angle (°)","a":"65","form":"val","o":null}],"hint":"Opposite angles are equal.","steps":"1. Rule: in a parallelogram, opposite angles are equal and neighbouring angles add up to 180°.<br>2. The opposite angle is also 65°."},{"text":"Four equal sides and no right angles. Circle one.","vis":"","self":1,"parts":[{"label":null}],"hint":"Equal sides, no right angles.","steps":"1. Rule: square = 4 equal sides and 4 right angles; rectangle = 4 right angles with opposite sides equal; rhombus = 4 equal sides; parallelogram = both pairs of opposite sides parallel; trapezium = one pair of parallel sides; kite = two pairs of equal sides next to each other.<br>2. Four equal sides and no right angles: a rhombus. Answer: B."}]}